From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 08:21:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smp2p: reset inbound state only on restart

SMP2P v2 needs cached inbound values reset when an SSR is detected
because the remote no longer waits for the acknowledgement before
setting its state. The current code performs that reset for every
inbound notification instead.

With persistent ready and handover bits, unrelated ADSP notifications
are therefore reported as fresh rising edges. This repeatedly invokes
the q6v5 handlers and can keep the AP awake.

Return early when the restart flag has not changed so the cached values
are preserved for ordinary notifications.

Fixes: 42c4cf5d4828 ("soc: qcom: smp2p: Add support for smp2p v2")
Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
index af0ceeaf6e07..89e242f4d0ca 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
@@ -194,13 +194,16 @@ static bool qcom_smp2p_check_ssr(struct qcom_smp2p *smp2p)
 
 	restart_done = in->flags & BIT(SMP2P_FLAGS_RESTART_DONE_BIT);
 	restart = restart_done != smp2p->ssr_ack;
+	if (!restart)
+		return false;
+
 	list_for_each_entry(entry, &smp2p->inbound, node) {
 		if (!entry->value)
 			continue;
 		entry->last_value = 0;
 	}
 
-	return restart;
+	return true;
 }
 
 static void qcom_smp2p_do_ssr_ack(struct qcom_smp2p *smp2p)
